{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now I understand the procedure. I need to:\n1. Create build scripts for both data sources\n2. Build and add them to the catalog\n3. Create a metric that calculates farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n4. Verify the result\n\nLet me start by creating the build scripts. First, I'll create the .xorq directory structure if it doesn't exist, then create scripts to ingest both datasets.\n\nSince we need to:\n1. Total farmers markets from the first CSV\n2. Get total population from the census CSV\n3. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n\nI'll need to:\n1. First ingest the farmers markets data\n2. Then ingest the census population data\n3. Then create a metric that joins them to compute the per-capita rate\n\nLet me start with the farmers markets script."}}
